{{!-- What a piece of loot is worth, spelled out ("2 gp 5 sp") instead of the system's
      number-plus-coin-glyph. A chest is scanned to decide what is worth carrying, and the
      glyph made every row end in a small icon that had to be decoded first; it also can't
      say "2 gp 5 sp" at all, only "2.5".

      The class must be item-<columnId>: dnd5e sizes columns with CSS keyed on that name for
      BOTH the header cell and the row cell, so any other name leaves the two out of step.
      Widths live in styles/lootshelf.css and match the shelf's price column exactly. --}}
<div class="item-detail item-lootValue {{#unless ctx.loot.valueLabel}}empty{{/unless}}"
     data-column-id="lootValue">
    {{#if ctx.loot.valueLabel}}{{ ctx.loot.valueLabel }}{{/if}}
</div>
